  "solution": {
    "text": "(p) ln <math> <mrow> <mi>&#945;</mi> </mrow> </math> decay,&nbsp;the mass number decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> and atomic number decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.<br />(q) ln <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>&#946;</mi> <mo>+</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> decay, mass number remains unchanged while atomic number decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.<br />(r) ln fission, parent nucleus breaks into almost two equal fragments.<br />(s)&nbsp;ln proton emission, both mass number and atomic number decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.",
